{
  "title": "AWS SAA Anki deck + AnkiConnect integration (gap-prioritized)",
  "content": "### Overview\nThis plan builds (1) a syllabus-mapped Anki deck template for AWS Solutions Architect Associate, (2) an initial ~150-card starter set across EC2, S3, RDS, IAM, and Networking, and (3) Python automation via AnkiConnect to add/update notes, detect weak items (retention < 75% or ease < 1.8), and prioritize gaps using filtered/custom study workflows and tagging.\n\n### Key design decisions\n- **Syllabus mapping:** use official exam guide domain weights to define **topic importance weights**; map to tags and/or subdecks.\n- **Card schema:** consistent note types (Concept, Comparison, Scenario) with required fields enabling programmatic updates and stable IDs.\n- **Weakness detection:** computed from Anki stats (ease factor + review outcomes) and persisted as tags + a generated filtered deck.\n- **Prioritization:** weak-tag boosting + topic-weight boosting to pull high-value gaps to the front without breaking Anki’s core scheduler (i.e., prefer filtered decks/custom study over rewriting SM-2 internals).\n\n### Deliverables\n- Importable **.apkg** deck (generated programmatically)\n- **Python scripts** using AnkiConnect for add/update + weak detection + prioritized review deck generation\n- **Docs** describing structure, configuration, and maintenance/extension patterns\n",
